[SIZE="5"][B]Inventory Companion User Manual[/B][/SIZE]

Inventory Companion is an Elder Scrolls Online addon for inventory transfers, item tracking, currency monitoring, and capacity alerts. This guide explains the current in-game controls and workflows.

[SIZE="4"][B]Open the addon and tracking editor[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST=1]
[*]In ESO, open [B]Settings > Add-Ons > Inventory Companion[/B] to change addon options.
[*]Open the tracked-items editor using [B]Open Item Tracking Editor[/B] under [B]Settings > Addons > Inventory Companion[/B], the tracker panel's right-click menu, its edit icon, or the key assigned to [B]Show/Hide Tracking Settings[/B] under [B]Settings > Controls > Keybindings > Inventory Companion[/B].
[*]Assign [B]Show/Hide Item Tracking Panel[/B] in the same keybindings section to toggle the tracker HUD. This changes the same saved visibility setting as [B]Show Tracked Items Panel[/B]; the panel can still appear temporarily while editing or interacting with items.
[*]The editor has [B]Edit Items[/B] and [B]Edit Groups[/B] buttons to switch views. Right-click the tracker HUD for quick display options.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Show currency and inventory resources[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST=1]
[*]In the addon settings, open [B]Currency Summary Panel[/B].
[*]For a currency, use its [B]Character[/B] and [B]Bank[/B] controls to choose which balances appear. Account-wide currencies do not have those location controls.
[*]Use the row's show/hide button to include or exclude the resource from the panel. Hidden rows appear under [B]Not shown in panel[/B]. Use the up/down arrows to change the order of shown rows.
[*][B]Show Empty Currencies[/B] keeps currencies with a zero balance in the panel. Turn it off to show only currencies with a positive balance in at least one selected location.
[*]Drag the currency panel to move it. Right-click it to toggle whether zero-balance currencies are shown.
[/LIST]

[URL=./currency-panel-settings.svg]Schematic of Currency Summary Panel settings, including location, Notify, visibility, and ordering controls[/URL]

The Currency Summary Panel and [B]Standalone Progress Bars[/B] are independent. The progress-bar settings let you show or hide a separate bar for backpack space, bank space, or a supported capped currency. Drag a bar to reposition it. Its advanced settings control warning and danger thresholds and the normal bar color; shared alert colors control warning and danger colors.

[SIZE="4"][B]What the Notify controls do[/B][/SIZE]

There are two different kinds of Notify settings:

[LIST]
[*][B]Item or group Notify:[/B] In the tracked-items editor, click an item's [B]Notify[/B] label to toggle an alert when the item is gained in the backpack. For a group, click [B]Notify[/B] on the group entry to alert for items matching that group's patterns. This is separate from [B]Show[/B]: an item can notify without being displayed on the tracker. Use the [B]Notify[/B] filter at the top of the editor to find entries whose notifications are enabled.
[*][B]Currency or capacity Notify:[/B] In [B]Currency Summary Panel[/B] settings, check [B]Notify[/B] on a currency or on [B]Backpack space[/B] / [B]Bank space[/B] to receive an alert when that resource changes. Currency notifications work even if the currency row is hidden. These settings are separate from item and group notifications.
[/LIST]

The item editor's [B]Show[/B], [B]Notify[/B], [B]Inactive[/B], and [B]Untracked[/B] filters control which entries are listed for editing; they do not themselves enable or disable alerts. Click the label or checkbox to toggle a filter. [B]Untracked[/B] adds currently carried or banked items to the editor so they can be added to your tracked list.

Currency and capacity alerts combine rapid changes into a single update and suppress startup/login changes. To disable one type of alert, clear Notify for its row.

[SIZE="4"][B]Track an individual item[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST=1]
[*]Open the tracked-items editor.
[*]To add an item currently in your inventory, right-click its item slot and choose [B]Add to Tracked Items[/B]. Alternatively, enable [B]Untracked[/B] in the editor. This will show ALL items you have, then you can just click [B]Show[/B] or [B]Notify[/B] on that item's row; this will add it to the current tracked list while enabling that option.
[*]In the editor, click the item's [B]Show[/B] label to show or hide it on the tracker, and click [B]Notify[/B] to toggle gain alerts.
[*]Click [B]Totals[/B] to include bank holdings in the displayed count. By default, the tracker focuses on backpack counts.
[*]Click the remove button on an item row to remove that item from the tracking list.
[/LIST]

[URL=./tracked-items-editor.svg]Schematic of the tracked-items editor, including list selection, filters, and item options[/URL]

On the tracker HUD, left-click a group header to expand or collapse it. Right-click the HUD to show/hide empty tracked items, switch between single-line and multiline names, or open the editor. The settings button beside the title's edit button opens [B]Settings > Addons > Inventory Companion[/B] directly. Both editors have an [B]Other Settings[/B] button beside their title that closes the editor and opens the same settings page. Under [B]Item Tracker Panel[/B] settings, [B]Tracker Title Size[/B] adjusts the regular-weight title and both buttons together (default 20, range 16-28), without changing item rows. The tracker visibility toggle hides the panel in inventory, bank, and editor windows as well as during normal gameplay.

[B]Automatic tracker layout:[/B] Under [B]Item Tracker Panel[/B] settings, [B]Tracker Group Threshold[/B] chooses when the flat item list becomes categories. [B]Maximum Visible Rows[/B] limits the item area (default 20, adjustable from 5 to 50); the title is separate. Wrapped names consume one row per displayed line. If the list is too large, the tracker first uses single-line names without changing your saved multiline preference. Wrapping returns when it fits again.

Left-clicking a category saves your preference for it to be open or closed. Manually closed categories stay closed across inventory changes, settings changes, and UI reloads until you open them again. Automatic height adjustments are temporary and do not change these saved preferences. On initial layout or relevant content/settings changes, the tracker restores categories you prefer open when they all fit. Opening a category that still exceeds the limit temporarily closes all other categories; otherwise they remain untouched. Changing a category's matching or display settings can restore it only if you prefer it open and it fits alongside the others. If an inventory burst causes overflow, only the one growing category that was already open is retained; if several open categories grow or there is no unique candidate, all categories temporarily collapse.

A category that is too large on its own, an oversized flat list, or too many category headers uses scrolling. Categories with more than 200 eligible items display an overflow message instead of their item rows; narrow the group's patterns to display its items. Summary counts still include all matching items. Use the mouse wheel or scrollbar; the title and its buttons remain fixed. The panel keeps the same width when the scrollbar appears: item names become narrower and counts shift left to make room. The panel also stays within the available screen height.

[SIZE="4"][B]Create and edit a custom group[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST=1]
[*]Open the tracked-items editor and select [B]Edit Groups[/B].
[*]Select [B]+ New Group[/B]. A new group is created and its name field opens; enter a name and press Enter or move focus away to save it.
[*]Select [B]+ Add Pattern[/B] to add a matching rule. Enter an item-name pattern, then move focus away from the field to save it. A green deposit (IN) icon before each row identifies an Include rule; a red withdraw (OUT) icon identifies an Exclude rule. Hover over the icon for an explanation. Use the small swap button after the pattern to change its kind; hover over the button to see what it will do. Changing a rule's kind moves it to the Include section or the Exclusions section below. A group includes an item when it matches at least one Include pattern and no Exclude patterns. For example, include [B]*treasure map*[/B] and add [B]*cyrodiil*[/B] as an Exclude to keep Cyrodiil treasure maps out of that group. Exclusions narrow only this group; the item may still match other groups or be tracked individually. Matching ignores letter case, and [B]*[/B] matches any part of an item name.
[*]Return to [B]Edit Items[/B] to adjust the group's [B]Show[/B], [B]Notify[/B], [B]Totals[/B], and [B]Group[/B] settings. [B]Notify[/B] alerts when a matching item is gained; [B]Totals[/B] includes bank holdings; [B]Group[/B] controls whether the rule is displayed as a group on the tracker.
[*]In [B]Edit Groups[/B], use the group action buttons to hide/unhide or delete a custom group. Resetting a predefined group restores only its name and pattern list to the current addon defaults. All display settings, including hidden state, are retained. The [B]Miscellaneous[/B] group is a special catch-all and does not have editable patterns.
[/LIST]

Only your edits to predefined groups are saved. Unmodified names, patterns, and display settings can follow updated defaults in future addon versions. Restoring an edited value to its default removes that override.

[B]Saved settings upgrades and rollback:[/B] This release upgrades saved settings from version 1 to version 2, preserving tracked items, group edits, and other settings. All stored account and character lists are converted at startup, including inactive characters. Back up your saved variables before upgrading. No automatic backup is created.

If saved settings require a newer version than the installed addon supports, the addon stops initialization with an error before loading or changing those settings. Install a compatible newer addon or restore a compatible backup. This protection only exists in builds containing the version check: older releases without it cannot safely read the new group format. To return to one of those releases, restore a backup from before migration; reinstalling the older addon alone is not sufficient.

[URL=./custom-groups-editor.svg]Schematic of the custom-groups editor, showing the group list and pattern rules[/URL]

[SIZE="4"][B]Use account-wide or character-specific lists[/B][/SIZE]

In the tracked-items editor, use [B]Use Character List[/B] to switch between the shared account-wide list and a list specific to the current character. The character-list preference is stored per character.

To copy another list into the active destination:

[LIST=1]
[*]Choose a source in [B]Import from:[/B].
[*]Check the preview to see how many entries will be replaced and imported.
[*]Select [B]Import[/B] and confirm the replacement.
[/LIST]

Import replaces the destination list and its rule overrides; it does not merge two lists.

[SIZE="4"][B]Deposit and withdraw crafted items[/B][/SIZE]

Assign keys for [B]Deposit Crafted Items[/B] and [B]Withdraw Crafted Items[/B] under [B]Settings > Controls > Keybindings > Inventory Companion[/B]. Open a bank or storage chest, then use the relevant key. The addon queues supported items crafted by the current character and reports transfer progress. It will not transfer items outside its built-in crafted-item list.

[B]Auto-Merge Chest Stacks[/B] in the addon settings controls whether matching backpack stacks are automatically moved into house storage chest stacks when the chest opens. This setting does not enable merging for the regular bank.

[SIZE="4"][B]Move part of a stack[/B][/SIZE]

With a bank, subscriber bank, or house chest open, right-click a stack with more than one item. Choose [B]Deposit 1[/B] / [B]Withdraw 1[/B] or the corresponding option for all but one item. These actions move only that stack quantity and are separate from the bulk crafted-item keybindings.

[SIZE="4"][B]Adjust tracker and transfer settings[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]In [B]Item Tracker Panel[/B] settings, [B]Show Tracked Items Panel[/B] is the master visibility switch. [B]Tracker Group Threshold[/B] determines when group headers are used; below the threshold, visible entries are shown as a flat alphabetized list. [B]Multiline Item Names[/B] and [B]Show Empty Tracked Items[/B] adjust the display.
[*][B]Item Transfer Delay (ms)[/B] controls spacing between queued bank transfers. Lower values may make transfers faster but can risk an ESO disconnect; keep the value conservative.
[*]In [B]Standalone Progress Bars[/B], each resource can be shown independently and has advanced threshold/color settings.
[/LIST]
